00:19:05,321 --> 00:19:08,120
a sort of pancake. It's like seeing the edge of a knife.

235
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:15,240
When the B-2 makes its maiden flight on July 17th, 1989, it flies every bit as good as

236
00:19:15,241 --> 00:19:15,941
it looks.

237
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:28,100
The B-2 has a 172-foot wingspan, is 69 feet long, and 17 feet high.

238
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:36,740
Weighing in at nearly 154,000 pounds empty and 375,000 pounds loaded, it is a monster.

239
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:48,980
Approximately 80% of its structure is made of carbon fiber composite, lighter than aluminum, stronger than steel.

240
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:58,380
Its four low-noise General Electric F-118 engines each provide almost 19,000 pounds of thrust.

241
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:08,280
They have special exhaust vents on the top of the wings, which, when its hot gases are mixed with cooler air, make it almost undetectable to heat-seeking SAMs.

242
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:19,755
With a top speed of approximately 680 miles per hour and a service ceiling of 50,000 feet, this massive aircraft also can fly approximately 6,000 miles without

243
00:20:19,756 --> 00:20:20,456
refueling.

244
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,300
No target anywhere in the world is safe from its weapons.

245
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:27,680
And the amount of weapons it can carry is awesome.

246
00:20:27,681 --> 00:20:32,620
40,000 pounds of conventional, laser-guided, or nuclear bombs and missiles.

247
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:38,280
The airplane can carry a variety of weapons, almost anything in the Air Force inventory.

248
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:41,160
Our primary weapons, though, are the guided munitions.

249
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:47,020
Our bread and butter is the GPS-aided JDAM, the Joint Direct Attack Munition.

