00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:43,480
Because the simulator is so intensive and realistic,

331
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,040
and because the V-2 is a global warrior,

332
00:26:46,041 --> 00:26:50,540
the crews are trained to stay in one for as long as an actual mission might last.

333
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:54,700
Those first simulators are all four, five-hour sims.

334
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,680
You eventually do a 24-hour simulator,

335
00:26:57,060 --> 00:27:01,040
and you really get to know what it is like, what flying the B-2 is about.

336
00:27:01,140 --> 00:27:05,460
It is not about getting out there, yanking and banking, sweating, pulling Gs.

337
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:08,620
It's about capably managing the systems

338
00:27:08,621 --> 00:27:12,440
to most efficiently drop on the targets that you've been assigned

339
00:27:12,441 --> 00:27:14,320
and then bring the jet home safely.

340
00:27:14,321 --> 00:27:18,160
You know, I'm not going to end up with the bill, but Uncle Sam is if something happens,

341
00:27:18,161 --> 00:27:22,160
and you want to be the best steward of this resource that you can.

